  "goodToKnow": "Das Waisenhaus is an orphanage, an old-fashioned word; today children who can't live with their parents go to a Kinderheim or Pflegefamilie (foster family). The Franckesche Stiftungen in Halle began in 1698 as an orphanage and school founded by the Pietist August Hermann Francke. Die Waise is an orphan (the word is feminine even for boys), and die Waisenrente an orphan's pension. Plural: die Waisenhäuser."
